CommitDate: Mon Nov 9 17:42:02 2026 +0000

    Recognise Act 26 pre-landing records in the Act 21 compliance checker
    
    Accept a state-delivery record as a third evidence source only when it is a
    complete Act 26 record: schema act26-prelanding-record/v1, commit/tree/parent,
    verdict pass, landing_authorisation, created_at (or board pin time), non-empty
    content_assertions with non-empty expected and actual values, the canonical
    sha256 recomputation, and a matching detached <record>.sha256. The record must
    name the exact change commit and tree. Chronology uses the next first-parent
    commit as the deterministic upper bound on the landing; a record for the
    current tip fails closed until a later commit exists.
    
    Existing Git and reviewed-merge receipt paths and the fcad7c9 batching are
    preserved. Compliant rows now carry the record filename in "source" and the
    source label in "source_labels" (git/receipt rows included).
    
    Literal-predicate conflicts recorded, not loosened:
    - acceptance criterion 1 lists eight 2026-11-08 landings, but criterion 5 and
      Act 26 s2.1(3) reject pre-schema or digest-less records. Of those eight only
      0ca9353 (record act28-codification-prelanding-c1a0000b.json) now qualifies.
      06c1da6, f854aad, a46258e, d93cc0e and 65da1b7 have pre-schema state records
      with no schema/sha256/detached digest; eec8d45 and 1f27be9 have no Act 26
      state record. act27's record carries a schema and an internal sha256 but no
      detached digest and its internal digest does not recompute under the
      enacted canonical rule, so it is rejected.
    - created_at is compared with the landing bound (the next first-parent commit),
      not the candidate commit's committer time: Act 26 verifies a candidate after
      building it, so the canonical 0ca9353 record (created 23:12:08Z) is later
      than the candidate's committer time (22:48:49Z) but earlier than the next
      main commit (23:18:12Z). Comparing to the candidate time would reject every
      valid Act 26 record.
    
    Hermetic test tests/suite-compliance-act26-record-smoke.sh covers the valid
    record, tree mismatch, late record, missing content_assertions/verdict/sha256,
    and the existing receipt positive control with zero violations.

